7/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343295" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$W(x)=0$ for all $x\\in R$"] ["text" "$W(x)=0$ for some but not all $x\\in R$"] ["text" "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x\\in R$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343295" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$W(x)=0$ for all $x\\in R$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{3}{x}{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(0,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(2)=5.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(2)=5,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{3}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{3}{x}W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-\\frac{3}{x}W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-\\frac{3}{x}\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -\\frac{3}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{x}^{-3} \\\\ W & =\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=5$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =\\frac{C}{{2}^{3}} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{C}{8} \\\\ C & =40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f2134f9d1dd8d88f385dff3c82df3dba46b6703acd8330ae8aa65574813ae536"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{3}{x}"] ["math" "-\\frac{Q(x)}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{x}{Q(x)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{x}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{C}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{C}{{e}^{x}}"] ["math" "\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{C}{{x}^{3}}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$W(x)=0$ for all $x>0$"] ["text" "$W(x)=0$ for some but not all $x>0$"] ["text" "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x>0$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-343299" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x>0$"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-342724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(0)=1.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(0)=1,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-342724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=2W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =2W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =2\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =2x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{2x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =C{e}^{2\\cdot 0} \\\\ 1 & =C\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)={e}^{2x}$ and $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x\\in R.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-342724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f2134f9d1dd8d88f385dff3c82df3dba46b6703acd8330ae8aa65574813ae536"} {"question" "q-342724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-342724" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-2q(x)"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2q(x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070717/state.json" "file_sha256" "69c5caa3276eac16badd5b9687f619f7626c9b6ffe63853dd701b59cceb35bb5"} {"question" "q-3